meta {
  name: Logout
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Clears the saidkick_session cookie and returns 204 No Content.
  No request body is required.

  The presented session's jti is recorded in revoked_sessions until the
  token's own expiry, so replaying the old cookie value afterwards gets
  401. A missing, malformed or expired cookie needs no row; the endpoint
  still returns 204. Sessions minted before the jti claim existed cannot
  be revoked and age out within one session TTL.

  Responses:
    204 No Content — session revoked and cookie cleared (Set-Cookie: saidkick_session=; MaxAge=-1)

  NOTE: In dev mode (APP_DEV_MODE=true) there is no session cookie — the
  DevModeAuthenticator uses the X-Dev-User-ID header instead. This
  endpoint is a no-op in dev mode (the cookie clear is harmless).
}
